    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (76.67) stands as our premier offensive anchor. Despite facing a southpaw in Rod\u00f3n, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** maintains an elite profile, benefiting from a prime #2 spot in the order and a favorable 4.31 xERA matchup, making him a must-start to capture his high-floor production. Joining him as a primary engine is **Bryson Stott** (72.46). **Bryson Stott** is currently thriving against right-handed pitching, and with a soft 5.32 xERA target in Scherzer, he holds the highest upside among our middle infielders. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** (66.94) remains a strong play; his ability to capitalize on the righty-righty platoon advantage against Sproat makes him our most efficient outfielder today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Geraldo Perdomo** (44.86) and **Masyn Winn** (44.02). Both were considered to bolster our SB potential, as we are prioritizing speed, but ultimately both were bypassed due to their unfavorable matchups against Gusto and Warren, respectively, and lower aggregate efficiency scores compared to **Gavin Sheets** (55.61) and **Taylor Ward** (55.54). **Taylor Ward** earns the nod primarily due to a substantial +16% park factor advantage, even though he faces a respectable arm in Kirby. We are playing a cautious game with **Luis Arraez** (45.30) and **Matt Chapman** (46.58); while their scores are marginal, their roles as core contributors keep them in the lineup, though we will be monitoring the Griffin matchup closely, as the southpaw\u2019s 3.79 xERA acts as a dampener for both hitters.\n\nBeyond the tactical lineup decisions, we continue to manage our overall game caps with caution. **Cal Raleigh** remains sidelined on the IL, and **Will Smith** is out of the lineup entirely, simplifying our catching situation. We are also keeping a close watch on **Jonathan Aranda** (50.14), who faces a challenging lefty-lefty matchup against Bennett; while his base projections are solid, the -12% platoon penalty is a non-negligible risk. With **Jung Hoo Lee** (40.91) teetering near the bench threshold, the margin for error today is thin, and we will lean on **Gleyber Torres** (59.17) to provide the necessary stability in the #2 hole to keep our 5x5 categories competitive.",
